[38;2;124;124;124mThe problem: Let $X$ be a projective variety and $F \in \overline{NE}(X)$ an [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mextremal face. A morphism $f: X \to Y$ is called the contraction of $F$ if:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $f(C) = \text{point}$ for an irreducible curve $C \subset X$ if and only if [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$[C] \in F$.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $f_*(\mathcal{O}_X) = \mathcal{O}_Z$ (wait, this says $\mathcal{O}_Z$ but the [0m[38;2;124;124;124mmorphism is to $Y$... probably a typo, should be $\mathcal{O}_Y$).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mQuestion: Is the contraction morphism $f$ proper?[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about this. $X$ is a projective variety, so $X$ is proper over the [0m[38;2;124;124;124mbase field $k$. A morphism from a proper scheme to any scheme is proper. This is[0m[38;2;124;124;124ma fundamental property: if $X$ is proper over $k$ and $f: X \to Y$ is any [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mmorphism of schemes over $k$, then $f$ is proper.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis follows from the fact that properness is stable under composition and [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcancellation. Specifically, $X \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ is proper, and $X \to [0m[38;2;124;124;124mY \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ factors through $Y$. Since $X \to [0m
